{title: Greensleeves}
{subtitle: Traditional English Folk Song (Public Domain)}
{artist: Traditional}
{composer: Traditional}
{key: Am}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 80}
{capo: 0}

{comment: This is the traditional public-domain version. 
Many lyrical variants exist; this one is historically attested.}

{comment: Suggested fingerpicking pattern}
{comment: | 5 - 3 - 2 - 1 - 2 - 3 |}

{define: Am base-fret 1 frets 0 0 2 2 1 0}
{define: G  base-fret 1 frets 3 2 0 0 0 3}
{define: C  base-fret 1 frets x 3 2 0 1 0}
{define: E  base-fret 1 frets 0 2 2 1 0 0}
{define: F  base-fret 1 frets 1 3 3 2 1 1}

{start_of_verse}
[Am]Alas, my love, you [G]do me wrong
[Am]To cast me off dis[E]courteously
[Am]For I have loved you [G]well and long
[Am]Delighting [G]in your [Am]company
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Am]Greensleeves was all my [G]joy
[Am]Greensleeves was my de[E]light
[Am]Greensleeves was my [G]heart of gold
[Am]And who but [G]my lady [Am]Greensleeves
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Optional instrumental interlude}
{comment: | Am | G | Am | E | Am | G | Am G | Am |}

{start_of_verse}
[Am]Your vows you've broken, [G]like my heart
[Am]Oh, why did you so [E]enchant me
[Am]Now I remain in [G]worlds apart
[Am]But still I [G]love you [Am]gently
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Am]Greensleeves was all my [G]joy
[Am]Greensleeves was my de[E]light
[Am]Greensleeves was my [G]heart of gold
[Am]And who but [G]my lady [Am]Greensleeves
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: End with a slow arpeggio on Am}
